 "notes": "This paper presents lattice QCD calculations of the equation of state and topological susceptibility \u03c7(T) to predict axion mass in post-inflation and pre-inflation scenarios. The primary result is a relationship between axion mass m_A and decay constant f_A (or initial angle \u03b8\u2080). Figure 3 shows the post-inflation scenario predicts m_A = 28(2) \u00b5eV as a strict lower bound, with a range of 50\u20131500 \u00b5eV depending on the dark matter abundance assumption. The paper does NOT present an experimental exclusion limit but rather a cosmological prediction/projection based on lattice QCD. The coupling_type is AxionMass because the paper's main result is on the f_a\u2013m_a plane itself (derived from \u03c7(T) and EoS), not a coupling constant like g_agamma. Data points encode the predicted mass range: lower bound ~28 \u00b5eV (2.8e-5 eV) and upper bound ~1500 \u00b5eV (1.5e-3 eV), both at f_a ~ 10^9 GeV (typical PQ scale). Confidence is moderate (0.75) because the paper is a theoretical prediction, not a measured exclusion, and the exact f_a values are not explicitly tabulated in the main text. | vector-trace candidate: chi3-eps-converted-to.pdf colour (1.0, 0.2, 0.2), 173 pts (selected among 10) | selector: vector_trace (sole candidate)",
